.claude/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
checkpoints/
logs/
experiments/*
!experiments/*.sh
!experiments/*/
!experiments/*/logs/
!experiments/*/logs/**
!experiments/*/results/
!experiments/*/results/**
# Per-round / per-arm sub-experiments (exp008/exp009 round_NN, pretrain-consol
# 17ch|26ch, ...): the bare `logs/` above matches at any depth, so the one-level
# negations don't reach them — but the docs read these jsonl at render time.
!experiments/*/*/logs/
!experiments/*/*/logs/**
experiments/*/checkpoints/
experiments/*/caches/
experiments/*/dumps/
experiments/*/scratch/
experiments/smoke/
experiments/*/logs/*.out
experiments/*/logs/stdout.log
experiments/*/*/logs/*.out
experiments/*/*/logs/stdout.log
# Per-chunk arena/GNUBG stdout (exp009 `arena_rNN_cN.log`, `gnubg_rNN_cN.log`):
# every completed chunk ends "Result logged to .../eval_log.jsonl" and is a strict
# duplicate of a committed jsonl row; the rest are runs killed mid-match with no
# result at all. Committing them would only invite the double-count that
# pretraining_analysis.qmd warns about at R15_BASELINE. Deliberately narrow — it
# must NOT catch pretrain-consol/logs/gnubg_round15_chunk*.log, which is the sole
# record of that n=200 benchmark and IS read at render time.
experiments/*/logs/arena_r[0-9]*_c[0-9]*.log
experiments/*/logs/gnubg_r[0-9]*_c[0-9]*.log
perplexity-conversation.md
*.html
*_files/
tmpclaude*
docs/bagai/
data/wildbg/
data/bglab/
data/distill/
data/bgsage/
